Approach:
As it says in the description itself to chek the metadata of this png on checking the metadata we see a poem:
"Crimson heart, vibrant and bold, Hearts flutter at your sight. Evenings glow softly red, Cherries burst with sweet life. 
Kisses linger with your warmth. Love deep as merlot. Scarlet leaves falling softly, Bold in every stroke."
If we see the first the letters of this poem are in capital on adding them to getter we get CHECK LSB. LSB also
known as 'Least Significant Bit' is a method of hiding data within the least significant bits of pixel values in an
image commonly used in steganography. we need to install zsteg using the cmd "gem install --user-install zsteg". 
Upon using zsteg red.png we see the LSB of the png file there is a text in base64 format which on converting in 
Cybberchef we get the flag as the output.

